Package: powerkit
Title: Unified Power Analysis for Psychology Designs
Version: 0.28.0
Authors@R:
    person("Joel", "Thornton", , "58643641+JoelThornton@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads a single design specification (JSON) for common
    psychology designs, checks that it describes a possible population, and
    routes it to established backend packages to estimate power, required
    sample size and sensitivity. This development version runs t-tests,
    correlations, proportions and chi-square tests (via 'pwr', 'pwrss' and
    'Spower', with Bayes factor t-tests via 'bfpwr'), one-way, factorial
    and mixed ANOVA, ANCOVA and planned contrasts (via 'Superpower' and
    'pwrss'), multiple, logistic and Poisson regression (via 'pwrss'),
    two-way regression interactions (via 'InteractionPoweR'), simple,
    parallel and serial mediation and first- and second-stage moderated
    mediation (PROCESS models 4, 6, 7 and 14, via 'power4mome'),
    cluster-randomised and multisite trials (via 'powertools'), equivalence
    and non-inferiority tests (via 'TOSTER' and 'pwrss') and structural equation models: model fit,
    measurement invariance, factor correlations and latent regression (via
    'semPower'), and planned meta-analyses (via 'metapower' and 'POMADE').
